{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"broke-boarish-hagfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nRemediation epic for the comprehensive quality audit recorded on ae1b-b2a0-a080-4b4e. Scope is deliberately narrowed to three buckets the audit flagged: (1) the CI default-suite reliability flake, (2) the assignee/user-facing documentation bug, and (3) the LOW-RISK, NON-OVERLAPPING slice of the file-size, complexity, and typing findings.\n\n## Scope selection (why these and not others)\nNon-overlap was computed against the file_impact of all 212 currently in-progress tickets (the audit ticket itself excluded). Every NEW child below touches only files with ZERO in-progress contention. Deliberately EXCLUDED:\n- High-risk complexity orchestrators `next_batch.compute` (CCN 42) and `import_ndjson.import_tickets` (CCN 45) — core scheduling/import logic, not low-risk.\n- The typing ratchet FLIP in pyproject.toml (contended by 9 in-progress tickets) and `runner.py`/`_config_schema.py`/`signing.py`/`_ref_lock.py`/`init.py` near-cap files (all contended).\n- Findings already tracked and out of the requested scope: mutmut lane (521b-04c3-572f-4514), repo-wide package DAG (44ea-43c6-b351-4d81), test-env hardening (def1-9c3c-6802-48bd).\n\n## Children\n- Adopted existing open tickets: fade-ea90-7564-4715 (CI flake bug) and 879f-5549-91e3-4d6f (user-facing doc drift incl. the assignee example).\n- New non-overlapping tasks: split near-cap modules structured_run.py / compact.py / event_append.py; reduce complexity of the graph blocker subsystem; annotate the attest package to be typing-ratchet-ready.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CI flake fade-ea90 resolved (or root-caused with a durable fix) so the Python 3.11 xdist worker no longer dies in test_opcert_service_app.\n- [ ] User-facing assignee example teaches a Jira-resolvable identity consistent with docs/config.md.\n- [ ] The three named near-cap modules are below the 500-LOC target, split only along existing call-graph seams.\n- [ ] The flagged graph blocker-subsystem functions are reduced in cyclomatic complexity with behavior preserved.\n- [ ] The attest package is clean under `mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs` (ratchet flip deferred to when pyproject.toml contention clears).\n- [ ] Every new child edited only non-in-progress-contended files.","id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["remediation","audit","ae1b"],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Remediation (audit ae1b): CI-flake, assignee doc bug, and low-risk non-overlapping size/complexity/typing debt"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786219904383770001,"uuid":"d49a9c28-ca0c-4927-a321-2e52d617b93b"}